WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.680
 It's like death staring at
you when you look at a camera.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.220
It's kind of scary also.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.830
I'm speaking to filmmakers,
our future filmmakers.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.940
You have to know I have
gone through all of this.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.770
I have learned it all on my own.

00:00:21.036 --> 00:00:24.230
[INAUDIBLE]

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:24.890
 Shit yeah.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.440
This is good stuff.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.440
And know there's
something I can pass on.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.140
For example, I do
not use a storyboard.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.705
I think it's an
instrument of the cowards.

00:00:38.427 --> 00:00:40.890
Acting, embarking with actors--

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.920
for me, it's chemistry,
understanding the world

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.600
and understanding human beings.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.670
Hold a camera.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.042
Don't look at the flip screen.

00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:50.790
Look through it.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.550
There's one book I
would ask you to read

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.128
if you want to make films.

00:00:57.128 --> 00:01:00.570
You'll spend way too much
time in the film school.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.530
It costs way too much money.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.925
You can learn the essentials
of filmmaking on your own

00:01:05.925 --> 00:01:07.290
within two weeks.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.170
And I see young filmmakers
who come excitedly at me,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.930
and they say, oh,
I shot 450 hours.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.440
My heart sinks.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.220
We are not garbage collectors.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.250
We are filmmakers.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.540
We are thieves.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.660
We get away with loot
from the most beautiful

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.925
or the most scary or the
most spectacular places

00:01:28.925 --> 00:01:31.090
that you can ever find.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.910
Just hit and run and
get away with film.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:39.200
I'm Werner Herzog, and
this is my Masterclass.

